<title>USA: Hanson shares debut after spinoff.</title>
<headline>Hanson shares debut after spinoff.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new version of Hanson Plc shares debuted on Wall Street on Monday after the company spun off its energy division and carried out a one-for-eight reverse stock split.</p>
<p>Hanson's American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) were trading at 22-3/4 in mid-afternoon. Volume was about 200,000 shares, only a tenth its normal daily activity before Monday's spinoff of the Energy Group.</p>
<p>Energy Group ADRs were up 1/2 to 37 on volume of 144,000. Hanson, once one of Britain's biggest conglomerates, completed a four-way breakup with the Energy Group spinoff.</p>
<p>Hanson said in a statement that its ordinary shares and ADRs would trade on the London and New York Stock Exchanges respectively in their new one-for-eight consolidated form. The ADR closed on Friday at 7-1/8.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
